          "fields": {
            "display_title": "This paper aims to propose a new GNN for heterogeneous graphs, which is scalable to large-scale graphs. The proposed idea is to leverage an existing model called SIGN, which simplifies GCN by dropping the non-linear transformation from intermediate layers, and extend it to heterogeneous graphs. The results on several benchmark datasets show the proposed approach is better and faster than baselines.",
